  "applies_to": "RTD-NET on the Daikin P1/P2 bus (VRV, Sky Air, VAM/VKM), up to 16 indoor units as one group; RTD-10 with the same firmware uses the same layout.",
  "summary": "Small Modbus RTU slave that joins a Daikin P1/P2 remote-controller bus and controls up to 16 indoor units as one group. Holding registers carry setpoint, fan, mode, louvre and on/off plus keypad lock modes and limits; input registers return group and per-unit temperatures, faults, filter and defrost state.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The manual states register base 0 and writes registers as H0010 / I0010 meaning wire address 10. Per-unit input registers are numbered unit x 100 + offset (unit 1 = 0120..0132, unit 16 = 1620..1632)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "RTD-NET Installation Instructions",
    "doc_number": "18870-1.06.03",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.daikin.eu/content/dam/document-library/installation-manuals/ctrl/RTD-NET%20installation%20instructions_18870-1.06%20EN_Installation%20manuals_English.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 6-11 (Modbus configuration, control, limits, VAM, readback, fault codes)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Every register is 16 bits. Temperatures in input registers are signed and multiplied by 100; setpoint and setpoint limits are whole °C (16..32).",
    "Only unit 1 of the per-unit block is listed. For unit n add (n-1) x 100 to each address (e.g. unit 2 return air = 223).",
    "Fanspeed inhibit (H0022) is listed without bit meanings: the manual's fan inhibit table (Low 2, High 13) does not follow the powers-of-two pattern of the mode and louvre tables, so it is not decoded here.",
    "Fault codes are two ASCII characters packed high byte / low byte (e.g. 16697 = 'A9'). The full Daikin code table is published by Realtime Controls separately.",
    "Function codes 03, 04, 06 and 16 are supported, 1..10 registers per request.",
    "The Modbus slave address is set 0..63 on DIP switch SW1."
  ],
